[CODE] STEP 1 — Make a new file: style.css in the beanforge folder. Type:

      :root {
        --coffee: #3b2418;
        --cream: #f5ead7;
        --copper: #b87333;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      body {
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        background: var(--cream);
        color: var(--coffee);
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      header {
        background: var(--coffee);
        color: var(--cream);
        padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
        text-align: center;
      }
      header h1 { font-size: 3rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
      header p { color: var(--copper); font-size: 1.25rem; }
      section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
      section h2 {
        color: var(--copper);
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--copper);
        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      }
      ul { list-style: none; }
      li {
        padding: 0.75rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(59,36,24,0.2);
        font-size: 1.0625rem;
      }

STEP 2 — Link the CSS to your HTML.
  Open index.html. Inside <head>, after the <title>, add:
      <link rel='stylesheet' href='style.css'>

STEP 3 — Reload your browser.
  Refresh the page. YOU SHOULD SEE: cream background, dark brown header, copper accent. Looks like a coffee shop.

