[CODE] STEP 1 — Open Chrome (or Edge). Open your Bean Forge page.
  Press F12 to open DevTools.
  Click the small phone icon (top-left of DevTools) — 'Toggle device toolbar'.
  Pick 'iPhone 13' from the dropdown at top.
  See how the page looks on a phone. Is anything too wide or too cramped?

STEP 2 — Open style.css. At the bottom, add this for bigger screens:

      @media (min-width: 600px) {
        header { padding: 6rem 2rem; }
        header h1 { font-size: 4rem; }
        section { padding: 4rem 2rem; }
      }
      @media (min-width: 900px) {
        #menu ul {
          display: grid;
          grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
          gap: 0 2rem;
        }
      }

STEP 3 — In DevTools, test these widths:
  iPhone 13 (390px) — single column
  iPad (768px) — single column, bigger padding
  Desktop (1280px) — menu in 2 columns

  Looks right? Move on. Looks broken? Tweak the CSS and try again.

